Say which lag bound throttled the pusher, and for which tenant.

Admission refuses an append for three different reasons: the tenant's
ingest is past its byte bound, its ingest is past its seconds bound, or
consolidation on the WAL shard is past the backlog bound. The pusher
logged all three as "consolidation is behind", so the one line an
operator has to work from named the wrong thing two times out of three
and never named the tenant (zou #255).

The Rust side already formats the exact reason, bound and tenant into
the error it refuses with, but the shim only handed C an error code. It
now keeps that text and hands it over on request, so the log line quotes
it: "zou wal pusher throttled: tenant 0x..., ingest is N bytes behind
durable, the bound is M". The reason is taken rather than
copied, because the line is logged once per streak and a leftover reason
would be reported again by the next one, naming a bound that had stopped
tripping. A pusher running against a shim without the call still logs,
just without the detail.

--- a/src/backend/access/transam/zou_wal.c
+++ b/src/backend/access/transam/zou_wal.c
@@ -49,6 +49,7 @@
 						 uint64 *out_resume);
 extern int	zou_wal_append(const uint8 *data, size_t len, uint64 pg_lsn,
 						   uint64 *out_durable);
+extern int	zou_wal_throttle_reason(char *out, size_t cap);
 extern int	zou_wal_durable(uint64 *out_pg_lsn);
 extern int	zou_wal_fold_start(uint64 redo);
 extern int	zou_wal_fold_poll(uint64 *out_redo, uint32 *out_dropped);
@@ -619,15 +620,26 @@
